Scheme name: ordmail

Status: provisional

Applications/protocols that use this scheme name:
On-chain mail applications on the ORDnet stack (ORDmail for iOS, with
the wire format deployed on BSV: mail carried as an on-chain OP_RETURN
envelope, optionally encrypted to the recipient's public key). An
"ordmail" URI opens a compose view with the recipient pre-filled;
sending is always an explicit user action. The scheme is deliberately
separate from "mailto:" — web2 and web3 mail actions are never mixed,
so applications can support both worlds without ambiguity. Specified in
ODNCA-STD-011 (public draft); this registration will be updated as that
specification is adopted.

Contact: Alexander Taytelbaum, ODNCA — ORDnet Decentralized Names
Coordination Authority, info&odnca.org

